that presented as a lump in the left testis. Involvement of which one of the following
lymph node groups by lymphatic spread would be associated with the worst
prognosis?','{"A":"OA. Cervical.","B":"B. Mediastinal.","C":"C. Retroperitoneal.","D":"D. Inguinal.","E":"E. Femoral canal."}','A','Testicular neoplasms spread via draining lymphatics along the gonadal veins in the
spermatic cord and along the inguinal canal to retroperitoneal nodes (option C) and
from retroperitoneal and para-aortic nodes; progressive spread can occur via the
cistern chyli and thoracic duct to mediastinal (option B) and left-sided cervical nodes
at the base of the neck. The latter group drain into the systemic venous circulation;
therefore, involvement of cervical nodes is associated with the worst prognosis.

Inguinal and femoral vessels and nodes (Cloquet) (options D and E) drain the leg and
the skin of the lower abdomen, back, buttock, penis, scrotum and anal canal. They do
not drain testes.','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[28],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-6dd3c099326a","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"0e783ff490d0d39fe6ea","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":28,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"d4c4d417d8c3f357b811","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_page":106,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"afe6b1a438aba6d0d817","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1937,"source_qid":"791"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"0e783ff490d0d39fe6ea","source_file":"Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":28,"supporting_pages":[28],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Renal/Urology","stem":"A 25-year-old patient is being staged for further management of a seminoma\nthat presented as a lump in the left testis. Involvement of which one of the following\nlymph node groups by lymphatic spread would be associated with the worst\nprognosis?","options":{"A":"OA. Cervical.","B":"B. Mediastinal.","C":"C. Retroperitoneal.","D":"D. Inguinal.","E":"E. Femoral canal."},"source_answer":"A","source_explanation":"Testicular neoplasms spread via draining lymphatics along the gonadal veins in the\nspermatic cord and along the inguinal canal to retroperitoneal 