the left testis. Which one of the following is the next best step in management?',NULL,'E','All scrotal lumps in a young male are malignancy until proven otherwise, especially if painless. Ultrasound is the
initial investigation of choice for assessing a scrotal lump. If a lesion within the testis is found on ultrasound,
malignancy should come at the top of the differentials list, and a blood sample should be obtained for serum tumour
markers. Tumour markers used for testicular cancer are alpha-fetoprotein (AFP), beta hCG, and lactate
dehydrogenase (LDH). LDH is usually elevated in metastatiic tumors.

In seminoma testicular cancers, AFP is never elevated and beta-hCG is elevated in less than 20% of patients. In
non-seminoma testicular cancer, however, AFP and beta hCG are elevated in 85% of patients. Serum tumour
markers, especially AFP and beta hCG, can provide evidence for the initial diagnosis of testicular cancer and are
useful for the assessment of the prognosis and risk stratification.

(Option A) Fine needle aspiration is not recommended for testicular cancers due to the potential risk of tumour
implantation in the scrotal wall.

(Option B) Surgical exploration is contraindicated due to the risk of tumour spread. Any scrotal incision should be
avoided. Once the diagnosis of testicular cancer is established, orchiectomy through the inguinal approach is the
best initial treatment.

(Option C) CT scan of the chest is helpful for tumour staging once the diagnosis is established.

(Option D) LDH levels rise when the tumour has metastasized and is not elevated early in the course of the disease
when no metastasis has occurred; therefore, this marker alone is not often diagnostic.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2025','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[31],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-456ad03f47dc","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"38d798eacf1ffa03a385","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":31,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"981dc47d6b7dc9ad04b9","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_page":77,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
