 or IVP (option A) unnecessarily puts the patient at risk of\nradiation and/or contrast media. Contrast CT scans, however, should be considered for patients in whom the\nsymptoms persist, or another diagnosis is suspected based on clinical grounds.\n\nA KUB x-ray (option D) is less accurate and only visualizes calcium-containing stones.\n\nTriple phase CT scan (option E) is mostly used for diagnosis of liver lesions. It is not indicated diagnosis of renal\nstones but may be considered if an alternative diagnosis","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","dose","drug","management","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"a3a90bf5917cd43402aeaca290e2e8d793b8c1bc","duplicate_group_id":"exact-a3a90bf5917c","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"90ea37bc79682538e47e","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":32,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"21d0541f7b8f648788f9","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_page":137,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"55904ef48644311fd12a","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_page":138,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.optio