the scrotum and testes."},"source_answer":"A","source_explanation":"A 2.5 times or more increase in serum FSH level indicates irreversible testicular failure. FSH is the most\nimportant endocrine test in the assessment of male infertility.\n\nSerum testosterone level is a helpful test in making a diagnosis of hypogonadism; however, its level varies\nin different age groups, and a low level does not necessarily indicate irreversible testicular failure. In\ninfertile men, testosterone levels are often within normal range.\n\nOther investigations, including LH (option B), inhibin, serum testosterone (option C), anti-sperm\nantibodies (option D), chromosome analysis, and an ultrasound scan of the scrotum and testes (option E),\nare helpful in assessing male infertility, but serum FSH remains the most important hormonal test,\nespecially in patients with azoospermia.","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"medium","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"b2a582cabf0c9784124198daf427f8b715dc3956","duplicate_group_id":"exact-b2a582cabf0c","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"51134e133b6e18eb37a6","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":36,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"76b6758b5e7b834a420d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_page":94,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"cba9efa017bf2c8b3af3","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook