regular timely unprotected sex for the past 12 months. Assessments on the wife''s side revelas no cause.
On male''s side, a semen analysis shows azoospermia. Which one of the following is the most important
next test for this man?',NULL,'A','A 2.5 times or more increase in serum FSH level indicates irreversible testicular failure. FSH is the most
important endocrine test in the assessment of male infertility.

Serum testosterone level is a helpful test in making a diagnosis of hypogonadism; however, its level varies
in different age groups, and a low level does not necessarily indicate irreversible testicular failure. In
infertile men, testosterone levels are often within normal range.

Other investigations, including LH (option B), inhibin, serum testosterone (option C), anti-sperm
antibodies (option D), chromosome analysis, and an ultrasound scan of the scrotum and testes (option E),
are helpful in assessing male infertility, but serum FSH remains the most important hormonal test,
especially in patients with azoospermia.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2025','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[36],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-b2a582cabf0c","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"51134e133b6e18eb37a6","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":36,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"76b6758b5e7b834a420d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_page":94,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"cba9efa017bf2c8b3af3","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1909,"source_qid":"575"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_jso