Despite recent controversy, since the alpha-1a selective antagonist tamsulosin generally has minimal side effects (unlike the non-selective prazosin), routine use
of 400 yg daily in conservatively managed of renal colic is recommended. Tamsulosin is not available on the Pharmaceutical Benefits Scheme (PBS) for the
treatment of urolithiasis. Alpha-1a antagonists are contraindicated in patients with end-stage hepatic or renal failure, and patients with severe orthostatic
hypotension.

Patients who are trialling conservative management should be advised to strain urine, to avoid unnecessary imaging if the stone has passed. Patients should be
given a specimen jar and asked to bring the stone in to be verified; the stone should then be sent for analysis. The stone should be palpated because
sometimes small blood clots may appear to be calculi on inspection.

Follow-up scans (X-ray KUB if the stone is definitely seen on the initial X-ray or CT KUB if it is not seen) should be organized four weeks after the initial visit
unless a stone has been collected and verified by the GP or urologist.

The following patients should be referred to a urologist or emergency department, depending on the situation, for further assessment and treatment:

¢ Patients who have Stones >7 mm

¢ Patients who have not passes the stone after 3 weeks of conservative management — renal damage risk increases after 6 weeks of failed passage

¢ Patients who have ongoing pain despite adequate oral analgesia — those with unbearable pain despite oral analgesia should be directly sent to the
Emergency Department

e Patients who have passed stones but have ongoing blood in the urine — for investigation of hematuria, preferably with three urine cytology tests and a CT
IVP

¢ Patients with signs and symptoms of urinary tract infection (UTI)

¢ Single-kidney patients.

¢ Patients with pre-existing renal problems

e Evidence of complete urinary obstruction such as anuria

This patient has a stone less than 7mm and has none of the above indications for referral or urgent invasive management; therefore, he can be treated
conservatively for now.

The urologist decides on surgical removal of stones (option E) for patients who fail conservative management or require urgent management. Available options
are ESWL (option A), ureteroscopy, and laser fragmentation of the stones with or without basket retrieval. A stent can be left in place for a few days (options B
and C).',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2025','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[37],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-204d4ddd2a9d","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"10540248411c2abbe763","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Renal &Urology amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":37,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"71adcf55b526fa479920","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Urology _ Neurology 1-40 .pdf","source_page":141,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"f12b86792ac33ee7788f","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1925,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,cu