with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD)?',NULL,'D','Right heart failure is a common complication of long-standing COPD. The underlying
pathophysiology is constriction of pulmonary vasculature resulting in pulmonary hypertension.
Pulmonary hypertension leads to right ventricular failure with the following features:

e Increased jugular venous pressure

¢ Hepatomegaly

¢ Ascites

S3 gallop (right-sided)

Ascites (rarely)

¢ Edema, particularly that of the lower limb

Of the given options, raised JVP is the most specific indicator of right heart failure.

(Options A and B) Although hypoxia and hypercapnia may become worse with right heart failure,
they often pre-exist as a result of COPD.

(Option C) Reduced FVC can be seen in severe obstructive and restrictive lung diseases. It is
not a sign of right heart failure.

(Option E) Hepatomegaly is often a late sign of right heart failure, but it may also be present in
other conditions such as portal hypertension, and is not specific to right heart failure.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2025','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Respiratory and chest amedex 2025.pdf","supporting_pages":[9],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-b7fbbdd96c76","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"efa02f2f98e998e827a2","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Respiratory and chest amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Respiratory and chest amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":9,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"422ea2407936eb403258","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_page":154,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"8d7a154f0e6609e9a102","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Respiratory  (1).pdf","source_page":155,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"5b8822e2a09e7289d08d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1788,"source_qid":"401"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image