and now has a PaO2 of less than 60 mmHg. The next step for this patient would be assisted ventilation either by CPAP or BiPA
(preferred), or intubation and mechanical ventilation.

Recommendations for oxygen adjustment for patients with an episode of COPD exacerbation is summarized in the following table:

_ PaQ2 (mmHg) = PaCO2 (mmHg) PH

eed Normal (36-44) or Normal (7.36- Reduce oxygen flow to maintain
(SaO2>>90% by high (>44) 7.44) or low PaO2 closer to 60 mmHg (SaO2
oxymetry) : (<7.36) 90%-92%) and monitor ABG

